<article class="env-lemma" id="0FK0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FK0">Lemma <span data-tag="0FK0">37.13.16</span>.</a> Consider a cartesian diagram of schemes </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X' \ar[r]_{g'} \ar[d] &  X \ar[d] \\  Y' \ar[r] &  Y }  \]
</div>
  <p> If $X \to Y$ is flat, then the canonical map $(g')^*\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{X/Y} \to \mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{X'/Y'}$ is a quasi-isomorphism. If in addition $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{X/Y}$ has tor-amplitude in $[-1, 0]$ then $L(g')^*\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{X/Y} \to \mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{X'/Y'}$ is a quasi-isomorphism too. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Translated into algebra this is More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0FJU" data-tag="0FJU">15.87.3</a>. To do the translation use Lemma <a href="/tag/0D0I" data-tag="0D0I">37.13.2</a> and Derived Categories of Schemes, Lemmas <a href="/tag/06Z0" data-tag="06Z0">36.3.5</a> and <a href="/tag/08E9" data-tag="08E9">36.10.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>